:"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#pullrequestreview-2791968604","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104787","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#pullrequestreview-2791968604"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104787"}},"submitted_at":"2025-04-24T17:19:03Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2866901602,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6q4XJi","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?u=24618295fece29a0bf5c850faf2555985232f5f2&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#pullrequestreview-2866901602","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104787","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#pullrequestreview-2866901602"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104787"}},"submitted_at":"2025-05-25T17:15:47Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2895941602,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6snI_i","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The correct code for meshes (both skinned or non-skinned) is in `GLTFDocument::_import_animation`:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\tNodePath mesh_instance_node_path;\r\n\tHashMap<GLTFNodeIndex, ImporterMeshInstance3D *>::Iterator mesh_instance_element = p_state->scene_mesh_instances.find(node_index);\r\n\tif (mesh_instance_element) {\r\n\t\tmesh_instance_node_path = scene_root->get_path_to(mesh_instance_element->value);\r\n\t} else {\r\n\t\tmesh_instance_node_path = node_path;\r\n\t}\r\n\tconst String blend_path = String(mesh_instance_node_path) + \":\" + String(mesh->get_mesh()->get_blend_shape_name(i));\r\n```\r\n\r\nNotice how we have keep separate track of mesh instances by node. We will need to do this for other types of objects as well. Traversing from the top of the node tree, through skeletons, is too unreliable. If there are other types of nodes than meshes, we may want to generalize the approach of keeping track of MeshInstance3D nodes to include other types too.\r\n\r\nI do not believe it is good form to hardcode `\"Skeleton3D\"` (I understand the old code was doing this, but so is the new code, and it is not correct). If this was absolutely necessary, I would ask for the skeleton's name, for example `gltf_skeleton->get_godot_skeleton()->get_name()` but I would prefer asking the mesh for its nodepath directly.\r\n\r\nMy experience writing code to traverse nodepaths, is that it is very difficult to write correctly and very error-prone, compared to using `.get_path_to()`","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#pullrequestreview-2895941602","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104787","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#pullrequestreview-2895941602"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104787"}},"submitted_at":"2025-06-04T09:12:51Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2908372150,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6tWjy2","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Remember that a single GLTFNode may correspond to multiple Godot Nodes.\r\n\r\nFor the case of skinned meshes, this is an improvement over what we currently have. However, it may break some cases where Node3D properties are animated. In particular, adjusting the translation, rotation or scale of a skinned MeshInstance3D which is also a bone should instead target the bone.\r\n\r\nTherefore we need to target both the \"component\" or sub-node of the Node. For example, the physics body for physics, or the Node3D, or the MeshInstance3D, or the light, because they might point to different places. For example the bone itself, or the MeshInstance child, or a child of a BoneAttachment.\r\n\r\nFor this reason, we need to add an extra argument to `get_scene_node_path` which can tell it which type of node we are looking for.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#pullrequestreview-2908372150","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104787","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104787#pullrequestreview-2908372150"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104787"}},"submitted_at":"2025-06-08T10:48:00Z","commit_id":null}]